 "summaries": [
  {
   "name": "Carnot 113 °C",
   "good": true,
   "text": "This heat pump delivers 375 kW of the 375 kW demand (100 %) at a COP of 4,76, drawing 296 kW from the heat source. It replaces 2.586.207 kWh/year of Electricity (boiler) with 472.255 kWh/year of electricity, saving 2.113.952 kWh/year of final energy and 302,1 t CO₂ per year. In the first year it lowers operating costs by 81.444 €. The investment is 585.938 € (0 % funding). It pays back after 12 years (2039). Over 20 years it earns 173.214 € in today's money (net present value, incl. 0 € residual value). Per kWh of heat the heat pump costs 7,56 ct against 8,59 ct from the Electric boiler (LCOH, annuity method, VDI 4646); static payback 7,2 years, internal rate of return 16 %. At 6 ct/kWh for Electricity (boiler), it stays profitable as long as electricity costs less than 16,94 ct/kWh."
  }
 ],
