  {
   "name": "Carnot 113 °C",
   "good": true,
   "text": "This heat pump delivers 375 kW of the 375 kW demand (100 %) at a COP of 4,76, drawing 296 kW from the heat source. It replaces 2.586.207 kWh/year of Natural gas with 472.255 kWh/year of electricity, saving 2.113.952 kWh/year of final energy and 302,1 t CO₂ per year. In the first year it lowers operating costs by 107.201 €. The investment is 585.938 € (0 % funding). It pays back after 9 years (2036). Over 20 years it earns 365.606 € in today's money (net present value, incl. 0 € residual value). Per kWh of heat the heat pump costs 7,56 ct against 9,73 ct from the Gas boiler (LCOH, annuity method, VDI 4646); static payback 5,5 years, internal rate of return 20,2 %. At 6 ct/kWh for Natural gas, it stays profitable as long as electricity costs less than 21,32 ct/kWh."
