   "text": "This heat pump delivers 203 kW of the 375 kW demand (54 %) at a COP of 5,67, drawing 167 kW from the heat source. The rest of the demand stays on the Oil boiler. It replaces 1.396.552 kWh/year of Heating oil with 214.306 kWh/year of electricity, saving 1.182.245 kWh/year of final energy and 177,5 t CO₂ per year. In the first year it lowers operating costs by 63.110 €. The investment is 316.406 € (0 % funding). It pays back after 8 years (2035). Over 20 years it earns 244.939 € in today's money (net present value, incl. 0 € residual value). Per kWh of heat the heat pump costs 7,03 ct against 9,73 ct from the Oil boiler (LCOH, annuity method, VDI 4646); static payback 5 years, internal rate of return 22,1 %. At 6 ct/kWh for Heating oil, it stays profitable as long as electricity costs less than 25,29 ct/kWh."
