   "name": "Butane_2 84 °C",
   "good": true,
   "text": "This heat pump delivers 105 kW of the 375 kW demand (28 %) at a COP of 7,48, drawing 91 kW from the heat source. The rest of the demand stays on the Oil boiler. It replaces 724.138 kWh/year of Heating oil with 84.269 kWh/year of electricity, saving 639.868 kWh/year of final energy and 101,5 t CO₂ per year. In the first year it lowers operating costs by 32.396 €. The investment is 246.094 € (40 % funding). It pays back after 7 years (2034). Over 15 years it earns 122.305 € in today's money (net present value, incl. 61.524 € residual value). Per kWh of heat the heat pump costs 6,58 ct against 9,43 ct from the Oil boiler (LCOH, annuity method, VDI 4646); static payback 4,6 years, internal rate of return 24 %. At 6 ct/kWh for Heating oil, it stays profitable as long as electricity costs less than 30,73 ct/kWh."
  }
